      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "9",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "9",
          "To consider 1. When describing noses, you can use the adjectives hooked, pointy, flat, button. 2. Lips are described as thin or thick. Also, full. 3. Eyebrows can also be described as thick, thin or bushy. 4. If you want to describe a piece of clothes, you need to follow the regular pattern of adjectives. The correct verb to use when talking about it is -wear- E.G. She is wearing a beautiful single red, silk, European nightgown. On top of it, she has a gorgeous, golden silk shawl."
        ],
